# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. .env is git-ignored; never commit it or paste it anywhere.

# Your domain. Point it at the server's IP address in DNS before the first start: Caddy asks Let's Encrypt for the
# certificate as soon as it starts, and that only works once the name resolves to this machine.
DOMAIN=looks.example.com

# The only required secret. Create one at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Web Push (optional). Leave both keys empty and the app never offers notifications. Generate a pair with the app's
# --vapid command (see DEPLOY.md, "Push notifications"), paste them here, restart.
Push__PublicKey=
Push__PrivateKey=
Push__Subject=mailto:you@example.com

# Moderators. Sign up in the app FIRST, then put that handle here and `docker compose up -d`: at start the app promotes
# the existing account with a listed handle (case-insensitive; it never demotes), and a listed handle can no longer be
# signed up by anyone, so listing it before you sign up locks you out of it. Add Admin__Handles__1, __2 for more people,
# each once they have an account. Or, at any time and without a restart:
#   docker compose exec app dotnet FitCheck.Api.dll --admin <handle>
# (--unadmin revokes; remove the line here too, or the next restart promotes it again). See DEPLOY.md, step 7.
# Admin__Handles__0=yourhandle

# Account recovery by email (optional). Mail is on when Host and From are set; see DEPLOY.md, "Email for account
# recovery", for the exact lines for Resend, Postmark and Gmail. The password is a secret. PublicOrigin is REQUIRED on
# a server once mail is on: links are built from it and never from a request's Host header, so without it no
# confirmation or reset link goes out on anything but localhost.
# Email__Host=smtp.resend.com
# Email__Port=587
# Email__User=resend
# Email__Password=
# Email__From=OREVOSH <hello@looks.example.com>
# Email__PublicOrigin=https://looks.example.com

# Plans (optional; the defaults are the pilot's). Every check is a paid model call: a visitor gets GuestChecksPerDay free
# checks with no account (per guest cookie and per address a day; 0 turns guests off), a free account FreeChecksPerDay,
# Pro ProChecksPerDay (never above Limits__ChecksPerDay, 30). ProPriceText is what the Pro page shows as the price.
# Plans__FreeChecksPerDay=3
# Plans__ProChecksPerDay=30
# Plans__GuestChecksPerDay=1
# Plans__ProPriceText=₪19 / month
# Plans__CompareNeedsPro=false
# A "no outfit in this photo" answer gave the person nothing: the first NoOutfitForgivenPerDay of them a day are not
# counted against the plan cap or the guest's free look (0 counts every one, as before Round 13). The global ceiling
# counts all of them regardless: each was a model call.
# Plans__NoOutfitForgivenPerDay=3

# Languages (Round 13). The UI languages that are live: only these are offered by the switcher, detected from the
# browser, and asked of the stylist; a browser in another language gets English. English is always on. Arabic and
# Russian ship in the repository, written by the builders and not yet reviewed by a native reader: enable each with one
# more line once someone has read its file (src/FitCheck.Api/wwwroot/i18n/<code>.json and the strings in
# Services/Localizer.cs), and restart.
# Languages__Enabled__0=en
# Languages__Enabled__1=he
# Languages__Enabled__2=ar
# Languages__Enabled__3=ru

# Billing (optional). Leave the provider at "manual" and grant Pro with
#   docker compose exec app dotnet FitCheck.Api.dll --pro <handle> <months|off>
# Switch to "stripe" only with a price and a webhook you have tested in test mode (DEPLOY.md, "Plans and billing"): the
# webhook endpoint is https://$DOMAIN/api/billing/webhook with checkout.session.completed, invoice.paid,
# customer.subscription.updated and customer.subscription.deleted. The three Stripe values are secrets. "Manage
# subscription" in the app opens a Stripe Billing Portal session, so save a Customer portal configuration in Stripe
# once as well (Settings -> Billing -> Customer portal), or that button fails.
# Billing__Provider=manual
# Billing__StripeSecretKey=
# Billing__StripePriceId=
# Billing__StripeWebhookSecret=
# Billing__PublicOrigin=https://looks.example.com

# The weekly flames board (optional; the defaults are the pilot's). The week opens at local midnight in TimeZone on
# WeekStartsOn (Sunday in Israel; the close is Saturday midnight) and the app closes it into the hall by itself. A fire
# counts only from someone with MinChecksToCount ok checks, an account NewAccountDays old at the fire, and up to
# MaxPerFirerPerAuthor fires per person on one author's looks a week. Set the zone and the day BEFORE the first week
# runs: the archive is labelled by them. The sponsor block shows on the board while Sponsor__Name is set; agree the
# prize first, --verify the account, and unset it when the week is over. See DEPLOY.md, "The weekly board and store links".
# Board__TimeZone=Asia/Jerusalem
# Board__WeekStartsOn=Sunday
# Board__MinChecksToCount=1
# Board__MaxPerFirerPerAuthor=3
# Board__NewAccountDays=2
# Board__Size=10
# Board__RisingDays=30
# Board__Sponsor__Name=
# Board__Sponsor__Handle=
# Board__Sponsor__PrizeText=
# Board__Sponsor__Url=

# Store links (optional). A tagged piece's link leaves through /api/items/{id}/out with no referrer; one line per
# affiliate programme you have JOINED maps the store's host to the query string appended there (subdomains included;
# nothing is appended for a host not listed, and nothing is stored on the link). Leave them out until you have joined
# one. The item sheet says "may earn a commission" under every store link either way (Affiliate__Disclosure is bound and
# not read yet; keep it true). The name carries a dot: fine for the app and for this file, but a shell's `export`
# refuses it; if your Compose version refuses it too, set Affiliate:Hosts in src/FitCheck.Api/appsettings.json instead.
# Affiliate__Hosts__amazon.com=tag=orevosh-20
# Affiliate__Disclosure=true

# Clips (optional; the defaults are the image's). The image ships ffmpeg, so new clips are re-encoded to H.264 MP4 in
# the background and play everywhere; the original serves until that is done. Set Transcode=false to turn it off, or
# FfmpegPath when the binary is not on the PATH. /readyz reports ffmpeg as a check only while Transcode is on, and
# /api/config publishes "transcoding".
# Storage__Transcode=true
# Storage__FfmpegPath=

# Logging (optional). One extra log line per request — the method, the path, the status and how long it took — on top
# of the usual lines. Off by default: a pilot's log is worth reading and this is a lot of lines. Turn it on for the
# first days of a launch, and off again once it is quiet. No body, cookie, header or query value is ever logged.
#   docker compose logs --since 1h app
# Logging__Requests=false

# ---- Round 13 - money: the spend meter, the daily ceiling and the alerts ----

# What a model call is ESTIMATED to cost, in USD per million tokens. SET THESE TO YOUR CONTRACT'S PRICES: the defaults
# in appsettings.json are the published list prices for Anthropic__Model at the time of writing, and every dollar on
# the numbers page and the daily ceiling below is built on them. `--doctor` prints the two in use.
# Anthropic__PriceInPerMillion=2.00
# Anthropic__PriceOutPerMillion=10.00

# The day's ceiling, in those estimated dollars, over a UTC day. 0 (the default) means there is none, and the doctor
# warns about it. SET IT BEFORE THE PILOT - 5 is a sane number to start with. At the ceiling every route that would ask
# the model answers 503 "the stylist is resting until tomorrow", before the call: nobody's allowance is spent, no
# guest's free look is spent, nothing is stored. It opens again at the next UTC midnight. Limits__ChecksPerDayGlobal
# stays beside it as the count-based brake.
# Limits__SpendPerDayUsd=5

# Where the app shouts when something is wrong, so you hear it before a user tells you: a readiness flip (and back),
# the spend ceiling, more than ModelFailuresIn10Min failed model calls in ten minutes, free space under DiskFreeMb, a
# backup that failed, and one line when the app starts. At most one alert per kind per hour. Set at least one channel.
# Webhook is any https URL that takes Slack-shaped JSON ({ "text": "..." }); a Discord webhook URL with /slack on the
# end takes the same shape. THE URL IS A SECRET: whoever has it can post to your channel, so it lives here and never in
# appsettings.json. Email goes through the same mail server as the recovery links, so it needs Email__Host/From above.
# Nothing secret ever travels in an alert: a name, a number and a setting's name, never a key or a person's data.
# Run `docker compose exec app dotnet FitCheck.Api.dll --doctor --live` to send one test alert down each channel.
# Alerts__Webhook=
# Alerts__Email=you@example.com
# Alerts__ModelFailuresIn10Min=5
# Alerts__DiskFreeMb=512
